00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:44,280
Michael, trust is the second most important thing a woman can give you, because

254
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:46,200
without it you can't get the first.

255
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,960
Eddie, come on, man.

256
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,400
She's been hurt before.

257
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,460
Not your fault.

258
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:57,100
Eddie, she's got a little girl.

259
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,720
All right, Mike, I see what you're getting at.

260
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:02,860
You feel it was a mistake for you to go to Parents Without Mates last night, and

261
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,120
you're right. Okay.

262
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:05,820
You should have gone to Parents Without Brains.

263
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:11,540
Yeah. Eddie, I saw your card downstairs.

264
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:12,940
Here's your change from the ice cream money.

265
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:17,260
37 cents? You wasted my 20 bucks on ice cream?

266
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,800
No, on my new CD.

267
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:20,760
Oh, no, no, no.

268
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:21,720
Don't give me that.

269
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:22,760
I'm not made of money.

270
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:25,900
Oh, Dad, you should have thought of that before you brought me into this world.

271
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:28,460
Hey, hey, hey, stop, stop.

272
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:30,000
Cut it out, cut it out.

273
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,320
Hey, get out of here.

274
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:35,780
Yeah, fungus. Hey, I'm talking to you two.

275
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:37,660
Oh, hey, fine.

276
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:41,300
I got some news that could cheer you up, but, uh, you're making me leave.

277
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:42,660
All right, no, all right.

278
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:45,720
Okay, okay. You know my girlfriend, Natalie?

279
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:50,280
Yeah. Well, I just found out she's got a daughter my age.

280
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:53,060
I think we're talking letters to penthouse here.

281
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:55,580
Get out, get out, get...

282
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:59,800
Get out. It's tacky enough.

283
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:05,820
No comment. Jason, wouldn't it be easier if we have this professionally installed?

284
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:08,840
Oh, Maggie, those guys get three, four hundred dollars.

285
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:22,080
Ben, move. I can't.

286
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:25,700
Come on. We're trying to lay linoleum here.

287
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,860
Well, then what'd you guys have me sand the floor for?

288
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:36,780
What's that? Um, my new CD.

289
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:38,940
Why'd you get the money to buy this?

290
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,400
Uh, money. You don't have any money, Ben.

291
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:45,640
Did I say I bought it?

292
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,180
I meant I stole it.

293
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:51,720
Hey, Mike. Yeah?

294
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,460
Where's that slimeball, Eddie?

295
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:57,440
Eddie? Uh, he just left.

296
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:59,140
Why? Was something the matter?

297
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,600
After what Ben told me Eddie did, a lot.

298
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,660
Uh, Eddie did something?

299
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:08,840
Oh, yeah. He actually paid Ben to pretend to be his son so Eddie could get closer to

300
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,140
this vulnerable, unsuspecting woman.

301
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,280
Can you imagine that?

302
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:17,720
I can. Uh, did Ben say anything else?

303
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:18,940
Oh, isn't that enough?

304
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,000
Oh, well, it is for me.

305
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:26,040
How's Ben supposed to learn to respect women when there's an example like that

306
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:31,740
around? I'm just glad that he still looks up to you, Mike.

307
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:35,060
I mean, you've really done some hair -brained things in your life, but you've never

308
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,940
done anything as hurtful, as scummy as that.

309
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,700
Uh, well, don't you think you've been a little strong, Dad?

310
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:46,300
Well, that's what you describe it, Mike, when somebody takes advantage of somebody

311
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:48,020
at their weakest moment like that.

312
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,820
I never really thought of it like that.

313
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:56,440
Uh, and I'm sure Eddie probably never thought it through, either.

314
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,200
That's nice of you, Mike, sticking up for your friend like that.

315
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:05,740
I tell you, I'm just glad that I don't have a son who would do something like that.

316
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,340
Mike, you're early.

317
00:17:20,820 --> 00:17:25,600
Hi. Look, Rachel, there's some things that I've been thinking about, and there's

318
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:28,320
something that I really need to talk to you about, and I don't think it should wait.

319
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,740
Rach, I can't find Judith's penguin.

320
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:33,360
Ah, this has to be him.

321
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,080
Yep. Mom, this is Mike Siever.

322
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:38,780
Mike, this is my mother, Betty.

323
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,000
Hi. Nice to meet you.

324
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,920
My pleasure. Excuse me, I'll just get Judith's penguin.

325
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:48,060
You don't look so goofy to me.

326
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,560
Oh, uh, she told you about that, huh?

327
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:53,940
You remember, Mike?

328
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:56,420
Remember, I've been talking about him all day.

329
00:17:56,620 --> 00:17:57,480
Where'd she go?

330
00:17:58,280 --> 00:17:59,480
We're gonna have such fun.

331
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,240
Say goodnight. Bye, Mom.

332
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:02,300
Bye -bye. Bye.

333
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:04,020
Bye, Mommy. Bye, Mike.

334
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:09,480
You're off. So, Mike, what was it that, uh, that couldn't wait?

335
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:14,280
Uh, maybe it can wait.

336
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,520
Okay, I'll go get my appetizers.

337
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:21,040
Okay. No, it can't wait.

338
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:26,580
Okay. Uh, get your appetizers.

339
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:37,780
Okay. Oh, my.

340
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:41,300
Can I, uh, get you something to drink?

341
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:46,040
Look, Rachel, I'm not who I said I was.

342
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,000
I've never been married.

343
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:52,060
Never been married?

344
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:56,260
No. It's okay.

345
00:18:57,960 --> 00:19:01,020
It is? You don't have to explain anything.

346
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:05,160
All that matters is the love I see between you and your son.

347
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:12,780
Ah, can I get you something to drink wine, soft drink?

348
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:17,120
Puffball. Look, my son is a girl.

349
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,020
Pardon? Yes, Chris.

350
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:25,800
Chris, it's my little sister Chrissy.

351
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:30,000
And Eddie, that sleazy guy at the meeting who I said I didn't know.

352
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,120
The guy that works for the CIA?

353
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:36,100
Yeah, that's the one.

354
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:43,740
Look, he thought it would be a good idea if the two of us went down to the Parents

355
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:45,780
Without Mates meeting to meet some girls.

356
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:48,780
So I went.

357
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:53,620
I'm not a father.

358
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:57,980
I guess I'm not much of anything.

359
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,240
Rachel, come on, say something.

360
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,400
You lied to me.

361
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,760
Look, I... No, I thought you were different.

362
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,920
Look, come on, Rachel.

363
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:19,080
I -I mean, I know you.

364
00:20:19,180 --> 00:20:21,840
You must have been through a lot, and I -and I didn't mean to hurt you, honest.

365
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:25,200
Well, nobody means to hurt anybody, but it still happens, doesn't it?

366
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:28,360
Well, look, you know, the easiest thing in the world for me to -for me to have done

367
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:30,420
tonight would have been just not to show up here.

368
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:35,560
You know, but the only reason that I am standing here acting like a complete fool is

369
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:38,500
-is because you mean something to me.

370
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:40,420
You mean a lot to me.

371
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:46,320
I mean, I really do care about you, Rachel, and...

372
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:48,100
I mean, can we just start over?

373
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:53,920
Please? What do you say?

374
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:58,500
My name's Mike Siever, and I'm not a father.

375
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:11,880
Thanks a lot, Dad.

376
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:12,560
It's a nothing.

377
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:13,780
What's wrong, Mike?

378
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,920
Come here. Sit.

379
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:21,640
You wanna know what's wrong?

380
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:24,200
All right, I'll tell you what's wrong.

381
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:27,740
Eddie's mad at me.

382
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,160
He is? Yes.

383
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:31,880
Because I told him how angry you were.

384
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:36,940
And? And... Well, he decided to go...

385
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:40,780
to go over to this girl's house in person and tell her that he was lying to her and

386
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:43,400
that he really didn't have children and ask for her forgiveness.

387
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:46,480
And it was really hard for him, Dad, because,

388
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:49,420
I mean, he was about to walk out the door, but he didn't.

389
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:55,640
I mean, he really wanted to start over with this girl with a clean slate because he

390
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:56,500
really likes her.

391
00:21:57,180 --> 00:22:00,500
What happened? She kicked him out.

392
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:07,240
Already. I mean, Dad, what else could he have done?

393
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:09,060
I mean, it should have worked out OK.

394
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:12,200
Well, you got to tell him, Mike.

395
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:16,080
You know, sometimes there are things in the adult world that just can't be fixed.

396
00:22:16,900 --> 00:22:20,980
But don't let Eddie doubt for one minute that he did the right thing.

397
00:22:23,620 --> 00:22:26,620
Yeah. Good night.

398
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:29,320
Good night. Oh, Mike,

399
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:32,400
something else you can tell Eddie for me.

400
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:42,440
Yeah? I'm very proud he's my son.

401
00:22:57,560 --> 00:22:59,240
Done growing pains?

402
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:04,000
Some girl finds you vaguely attractive, and you're about to turn her down?

403
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:06,300
Well... Let me put it this way.

404
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:07,900
Did Mr. Haley say,

405
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:09,860
I'll wait for the next comet?

406
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:16,780
You really told him not to buckle the peer pressure, to stand up to his friends and

407
00:23:16,780 --> 00:23:17,520
do the right thing?

408
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:21,700
Yeah. And besides, if she's really desperate, the weenie might get lucky.
